---
description: Logos Scripture Graph low-risk chunking delegation rule for Cursor.
globs:
  - "**/*"
alwaysApply: false
---

Before chunking, review-packet, route, evaluator, graph, retrieval, vector, or source-metadata work,
read `.ai/control/cursor_low_risk_chunking_handoff.yaml` and run `/chunking-preflight`.

Cursor may do compute-heavy review preparation only when Lowell or Codex supplies one exact target
from the T402 queue and the status is `ready_for_review_packet`. Cursor must not choose the target.

Stop on any request to change raw/canonical/processed/derived data, chunk output, route/evaluator
behavior, reviewed gold, child spans, graph edges, retrieval truth, embeddings, vector indexes,
boundary imports, source/manuscript rows, backend choices, profile promotions, canon scope,
preferred readings/source traditions, or theology authority.
